sessment, recommending tools like the Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool (MUST) and the Mini Nutritional Assessment (MNA) for identifying malnutrition risk, particularly in elderly and frail individuals.\n\nIn addition to its focus on clinical guidelines, ESPEN supports projects addressing hospital malnutrition and offers scholarships to enhance nutritional practices in healthcare settings. The organization also provides recommendations for nutritional interventions in patients with special needs, such as those with dementia, and promotes the use of immunomodulatory formulas for patients undergoing cancer surgery.\n\nESPEN's guidelines cover a wide range of topics, including preoperative nutritional support, management of acute intestinal failure, and hydration relevant to diabetes management. The organization is committed to evidence-based practices and regularly publishes consensus papers and research findings to inform healthcare professionals about the latest developments in clinical nutrition.\n\nOverall, ESPEN plays a crucial role in shaping the standards of nutritional care in Europe, ensuring that healthcare providers have access to the latest evidence and recommendations to support their patients' nutritional needs effectively.", "GIL A:Gil A is an author of the \"Tratado de Nutrición\" which discusses various aspects of nutrition.", "NUTRICIÓN Y DISFAGIA:Nutrición y disfagia is a topic discussed in the context of managing dysphagia through nutritional strategies.)<|COMPLETE|>", "VIDEOENDOSCOPIA DE LA DEGLUCIÓN:The \"VIDEOENDOSCOPIA DE LA DEGLUCIÓN\" is a diagnostic procedure that allows for the observation of the swallowing phase in patients, which is crucial for diagnosing oropharyngeal dysphagia. This technique involves both static and dynamic assessments of the anatomical structures involved in the swallowing process. It was first described by Dr. Susan Langmore in 1988 and is utilized to evaluate swallowing function and anatomy in patients experiencing difficulties with swallowing. The procedure is conducted in specialized units, such as the UFDOF unit, ensuring a comprehensive evaluation of the patient's swallowing capabilities."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}